From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bpereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 14:22:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Drop box state under subtrees that become display:none

Stylo clears the styles under an element that becomes display:none, but
its descendants kept their inline layouts, layout output, child lists
and anonymous blocks until the subtree was shown again. Release them
when damage propagation sees the root restyled to display:none; showing
it again rebuilds them.

getComputedStyle still reports elements in such a subtree by resolving
their style on demand (resolve_undisplayed_style). Run that inside the
layout thread state, because dropping its thread-local style context
runs queued sequential tasks.

Signed-off-by: bpereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
